    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0743" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 611.419/92</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-12-14">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6:45 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>1259. Sir Edward Grey informs me that the British Government will not issue
                    further licenses for the supply of manganese to the Carnegie Steel Company, the
                    Teneriffe Steel Company, and the United States Steel Products Company, as it
                    seems evident that any shortage of this substance from which these companies may
                    be suffering is due to their having sold their previous stocks to the German
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
